# Principle 15 — public pages are the product

graft is a public Apache-2.0 project. Every session follows
[docs/principles.md](docs/principles.md) without the user restating it.

README, `docs/install.md`, `docs/packaging.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, GitHub
release notes, and `docs/README.md` describe the software as it is.
English is the only README.

Do not put on those pages: pkg.bot, Repology coverage counts, eonik GTM,
lead lists, living submission boards, founder checklists, "waiting on
you", or "replace the editor" copy. Do not link `docs/SUBMISSIONS.md`
from them.

`dist/` recipes are packager source, not listings. A spec in-tree is not
`dnf install graft`.

```markdown
<!-- BAD -->
Packager recipes for the [pkg.bot](https://pkg.bot/repos) families live
in dist/. Living board: docs/SUBMISSIONS.md.

<!-- GOOD -->
Install from GitHub Releases, the Homebrew tap, or cargo --git.
Packager recipes live in dist/; a recipe is not a distro listing.
```
